WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.033
-Looking sharp, bud.
Thanks so much

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:02.734
for coming back to the show.

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:03.834
-Thanks for having me.

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:05.267
-You know, we had Kate McKinnon

00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:06.400
out here just now.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.167
-I know.
-Yeah, and I was like,

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:09.634
"Well, maybe they know
each other."

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:11.467
We like to see
if our guests know each other.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:13.133
-We have quite a history.

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:14.567
[ Laughter ]
-You certainly do.

00:00:14.567 --> 00:00:16.567
This is a picture of you.
You met at the

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:18.501
Independent Spirit Awards.
Is that correct?

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:21.200
-This is our first time meeting.
-[Both] Yeah.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.601
-And this is a picture
of Kate coming by you.

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:26.400
This is during her monologue,
maybe, or something.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.901
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:00:27.901 --> 00:00:29.200
That's a mouthful of ham.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.801
[ Laughter ]
Remember that.

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:32.434
-She has ham in her mouth?

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:35.801
She has ham in her mouth
and then this happened.

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:37.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:39.167
[ Cheering ]
-Yeah. Ahem.
-Wow.

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:40.667
Yeah.
The reason she's not out here

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:42.701
is, that night,
we promised each other

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:44.200
we would never see
each other again

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:45.767
[ Laughter ]
because we knew

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:47.601
we would destroy
each other's lives.

00:00:47.601 --> 00:00:49.267
-Yeah, of course, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:52.334
-Wow, that's getting to know
someone right there, Paul.

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:55.000
-I miss the simpler days,
when you could just

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.901
kiss a stranger
with a mouth full of him.

00:00:56.901 --> 00:00:58.434
[ Laughter and cheering ]
-Thank you.

00:00:58.434 --> 00:01:00.701
Not the first time I heard that.
Yeah, right. Yeah.

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:03.167
-Hasn't flown the past
couple of years, yeah.

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:05.300
-Pal, I saw "The Batman"
the other night

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:06.901
and you are fantastic
-Thank you.

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:08.968
in this as The Riddler.
The reviews are great,

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.267
by the way.
Congratulations on that.
-Thank you.

00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:12.300
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Great reviews.
-Thanks.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.400
-I knew you were going
to nail it.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:15.968
But how did this come about?

00:01:15.968 --> 00:01:18.334
Did you kind of petition
for this or they wanted you?

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:20.033
-No, I actually didn't know much
about it

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:21.601
and I got a weekend phone call,

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:23.534
which is always sort of good
or bad news,

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:25.033
you know, the weekend phone
call from work.

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:27.534
And I was actually backing
out of a driveway

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:29.801
with my wife next to me
and my dad in the back seat.

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:31.534
And the call came up
on Bluetooth.

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:32.767
It was my agent
and I was like,

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:33.934
"I'm not going to get this.
It's the weekend."

00:01:33.934 --> 00:01:36.000
And Zoe was like,
"Pick up the phone."

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.534
Pick up the phone
and it's like, you know,

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:39.167
"Matt Reeves wants
to talk to you

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:42.200
about playing The Riddler
and it looks," you know --

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.167
And when I hear good news,
I kind of just shut down.

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:45.767
I was like, "Okay. Okay.

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:47.167
[ Laughter ]
Okay. Okay."

00:01:47.167 --> 00:01:48.334
So I hung up the phone
and Zoe's like,

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:49.501
"Oh, my God.
What happened?

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:51.100
Like, what's wrong?"
You know, and I was like,

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.934
'I think they want me
to play The Riddler."

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:56.367
And she started freaking out
and I was freaking out.

00:01:56.367 --> 00:01:57.834
My dad's in the back seat
and he's like,

00:01:57.834 --> 00:01:59.701
"What's so exciting up there?"

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:02.267
[ Laughter ]
And I didn't want to tell him

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:03.734
because it wasn't totally
in the bag yet,

00:02:03.734 --> 00:02:06.601
but also my dad has me
on like Google alert.

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:08.734
He calls his friends
about stuff.

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:09.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:11.234
And I didn't want him to be like

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:12.234
the leak, you know...

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:14.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:15.868
...before it was all good.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:17.567
-So you had to lie to your dad?
-I had to lie to my dad.

00:02:17.567 --> 00:02:19.734
But we had this
two-hour car ride,

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:20.734
where, the whole time,

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:22.133
Zoe and I are going like,
"[Bleep]."

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:23.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:24.868
And my dad's, "What's going on?"

00:02:24.868 --> 00:02:27.100
And then I knew, when we got
back to my parents' house --

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.367
we were visiting --

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:29.901
he was trying
to figure it out online

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:32.133
[ Laughter ]
and he couldn't.

00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:34.467
-And then like a week later,
I could tell him, but, yeah.

00:02:34.467 --> 00:02:38.567
-Well, here's a picture of you
as The Riddler and this is --

00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:40.968
look at how frightening this is.

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:42.200
[ Cheering and oohs ]
-[Both] Yeah.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.601
When did you find out
you weren't going to be

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:45.534
a Riddler that wore like

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:47.334
an outfit
with question marks on it?

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:50.167
[ Laughter ]
-Well, my agent,
who's backstage,

00:02:50.167 --> 00:02:52.501
just reminded me that the first
thing I said to him

00:02:52.501 --> 00:02:54.534
after I read the script was,

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:56.567
"There ain't any green spandex
in this one."

00:02:56.567 --> 00:02:58.200
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, no, no.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.534
This is dark.
-Yeah, no.

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:02.868
The first time I read
the script, I mean, Matt Reeves,

00:03:02.868 --> 00:03:06.467
it is a completely singular
vision he's got for this thing.

00:03:06.467 --> 00:03:08.767
I was totally blown away
by the script, which, frankly,

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:10.767
I wasn't expecting to be.

00:03:10.767 --> 00:03:12.033
Given that it's
a superhero film,

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:14.300
there are so many,
I felt so lucky like

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.167
I get to do this one because I
thought it was so good

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:21.067
and it's an interesting take
on the character.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.667
-Yeah, it's dark.

00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:25.934
Did you get to bring any
of your own ideas to this?

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:27.701
-Yeah, sure.
-Was the mask your thing?

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:29.434
-Yeah, okay, so there's
kind of like

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:30.868
a vigilante thing here, right?

00:03:30.868 --> 00:03:34.133
Maybe my character doesn't
quite have the same resources

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:36.267
as, say,
another vigilante and so

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:40.133
[ Laughter ]
it's kind of more
of a home grown costume.

00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:42.634
and I wanted --
-It's a very interesting
take, yeah.

00:03:42.634 --> 00:03:44.367
-Yeah, yeah, so I wanted like.

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:46.000
He still needs to be able to go
out in the day,

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:46.968
a la Bruce Wayne, right?

00:03:46.968 --> 00:03:48.167
So I couldn't shave all the hair

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:49.501
off my body for like DNA.

00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:52.267
I wanted the details covered.
He's super meticulous.

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:54.734
So I had this idea
of like wrapping myself in --

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:55.934
I have to call it cling wrap

00:03:55.934 --> 00:03:58.467
because I think the Saran people
don't want

00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:00.567
[ Laughter ]
any legal association

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:02.834
with my Riddler.

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:04.634
[ Laughter ]
I wrapped myself in cling wrap,

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:07.133
which kind of looks scary,
you know, with the light.

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:08.901
And I thought, "Okay,
now I'm not going to shed

00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:10.434
any hairs here
on these crime scenes."

00:04:10.434 --> 00:04:14.901
And then, the first day
of filming, about an hour in,

00:04:14.901 --> 00:04:20.167
I just start to see white
and colors and my brain is --

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:22.067
things are getting very --
And it's day one,

00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:24.567
so you don't want to be the
actor who's like...

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:26.868
-Complaining?
-...yeah, "I've got a little
headache here,

00:04:26.868 --> 00:04:27.834
a little problem," you know.

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.667
-Sweating?
-You kind of suck it up.

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:31.667
You know, you can't sweat.
That's the issue.

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:34.701
It's like going back
inside of you.

00:04:34.701 --> 00:04:37.334
[ Laughter ]
-It's so clingy.

00:04:37.334 --> 00:04:38.734
-It's so sealed.

00:04:38.734 --> 00:04:41.400
So I made it through day one
without telling anybody

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.200
that I was like --
and I got home that night

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.634
and I'm probably Googling
"brain swelling" in my bed

00:04:45.634 --> 00:04:47.934
[ Laughter ]
and I'm like,
"Okay, is this a problem?"

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:49.734
And then, you know.
Or I was like,

00:04:49.734 --> 00:04:51.100
"Is this the character?
Oh, my God,

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.834
this is going to be
a long shoot," you know?

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:54.968
-Yeah, exactly.
-And then the next day,

00:04:54.968 --> 00:04:58.234
we just started to poke
some holes in the cling wrap.

00:04:58.234 --> 00:05:01.033
My head could breathe.
Things got a little better.

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:03.167
And I might as well take
this opportunity

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:06.167
to offer a disclaimer
to any Halloween costumers

00:05:06.167 --> 00:05:08.267
or cosplay fans out there --

00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:10.067
maybe skip the cling wrap.

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:11.834
[ Laughter ]
-You don't need to do
the cling wrap

00:05:11.834 --> 00:05:14.367
to be your Riddler.
-Yeah.

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:16.901
-Yeah.

00:05:16.901 --> 00:05:19.400
It's amazing,
your transformation

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:22.601
and how you do this guy
because he's creepy, man,

00:05:22.601 --> 00:05:24.167
and it's scary
and it's frightening.

00:05:24.167 --> 00:05:25.834
And I go, "Oh,
this is how he's playing this,"

00:05:25.834 --> 00:05:27.868
and I go,
"This is a dark Batman."

00:05:27.868 --> 00:05:30.667
But the idea is that
it's Batman's only second year

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:32.167
being the Batman.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:32.167 --> 00:05:34.934
-And so the cops don't really
know if they can trust him.

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:38.033
The public doesn't know
if they can trust.

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:40.801
-And it also kind of turns
morality on its head.

00:05:40.801 --> 00:05:44.100
So, yeah, it's like
an immersive action spectacle

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:47.334
that's also
a serial killer mystery,

00:05:47.334 --> 00:05:49.801
psychological thriller,
horror film.

00:05:49.801 --> 00:05:51.100
-Yeah. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.000
You got to go see it
on the biggest screen you can.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.501
I think it's --
I really like it.

00:05:55.501 --> 00:05:57.968
-It's beautifully shot
and it's so well done, bud.

00:05:57.968 --> 00:06:01.834
And this is the scene
I really wanted to show

00:06:01.834 --> 00:06:04.033
-Great.
-because this is just Paul Dano

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:06.167
at his best, showing you how
to do it, man. I love it.

00:06:06.167 --> 00:06:07.534
Here's Paul Dano
in "The Batman."

00:06:07.534 --> 00:06:08.667
Take a look at this.

00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:11.767
[ Suspenseful music plays ]
[ Rain falling ]

00:06:11.767 --> 00:06:21.300
♪♪

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:23.234
[ Indistinct voice on TV ]

00:06:23.234 --> 00:06:25.133
[ Door opens ]
-Police!

00:06:25.133 --> 00:06:26.968
Hands up!

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:27.834
-Ah-choo!

00:06:27.834 --> 00:06:29.167
♪♪

00:06:29.167 --> 00:06:31.067
-He said, put your
[audio drop] hands up,

00:06:31.067 --> 00:06:32.033
you son of a [audio drop].

00:06:32.033 --> 00:06:35.667
♪♪

00:06:35.667 --> 00:06:37.868
[ Stool creaking ]

00:06:37.868 --> 00:06:42.067
♪♪

00:06:42.067 --> 00:06:45.133
[ Creaking ]

00:06:45.133 --> 00:06:51.200
♪♪

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:52.434
-Yeah!

00:06:52.434 --> 00:06:54.601
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ Laughs ]

00:06:54.601 --> 00:06:55.901
Paul Dano, everybody.

00:06:55.901 --> 00:06:59.968
"The Batman" is in theaters
and IMAX this Friday.

